/-
CDCert.K6.OptSem — GENERATED (Claude's generator `mkoptsem.py`): **the option masks mean their options**.
The kernel checks of `CDCert.K6.Seven.C7O0`–`C7O5` give each option mask as `maskOfK` of the packed
comparisons and the option's code; with `cm7_0_eq`, `cm7_2_eq` and `maskOfK_eq`, `evalD_cmpOf` this is
`mkS1 d` (`mkS3 d`): the mask over `copy1` (`copy3`) of the option `d` of `groupsD7`, shifted by 64.

* `oc1_sem_n`, `oc3_sem_n`: the 273 + 273 options;
* `ocG1_sem`, `ocG3_sem`: `ocG1 = groupsD7.map (·.map mkS1)` and `ocG3 = groupsD7.map (·.map mkS3)`.

The comparisons are made at the level of the options (`mkS1 d` against `mkS1 d'`), so the kernel does
not evaluate any mask.

Part of the Lean formalisation of the Moros–Riis upper bounds for Condorcet
domains (deletion/gap framework originated by Pavlos Moros; improved bounds and
further mathematical improvements led by Søren Riis).

Lean 4.26.0, core only. No `sorry`, no custom axioms, no `native_decide`.
